<h1>Dr. Terry Flood, DHA, DBA, MBA, MS, MS, MS</h1>
<p class="contact">Pflugerville, TX | 254-319-8460 | mr.terryflood@gmail.com</p>
<p class="contact">The Collaborative Advocate Foundation | EIN: 41-3618003</p>

<h2>Project Role: President / Principal Investigator</h2>

<p>Founder of The Collaborative Advocate Foundation (TCAF), a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization built to dismantle structural barriers to health, economic mobility, and community wellbeing for BIPOC communities. After 20 years of military service including three combat deployments and a career in federal public health across VA and DoD systems, founded TCAF to answer a question the existing system never asked: what happens when someone who has lived through the barriers builds the solution from scratch? Personally designed, built, and deployed a 24-platform digital ecosystem serving Central Texas communities across health equity, workforce development, education, veteran services, and SDOH navigation. Brings deep expertise in implementation science (Dartmouth, Geisel School of Medicine), value-based care, crisis intervention systems, and AI-powered community health navigation. Certified Community Health Worker Instructor with direct experience training Veterans Crisis Line responders, implementing behavioral health programs at the population level, and designing community resilience frameworks for military installations.</p>

<h2>Relevance to Sankofa Knowledge Systems Project</h2>

<ul>
<li>Designed and built the 24-platform technology ecosystem that serves as the operational foundation for the Sankofa Health Network, including four AI engines (RAG knowledge base, Bidirectional Planning, SDOH Analytics, Community Intelligence)</li>
<li>Developed the RPLICE implementation science engine integrating eight federal data sources (CDC PLACES, Census ACS, EPA EJScreen, SVI, USDA, HUD, SAMHSA, BLS) for census-tract-level disparity mapping -- the same infrastructure that will index diaspora health knowledge against SDOH conditions</li>
<li>Created and deployed six validated clinical screening instruments (PHQ-9, GAD-7, C-SSRS, PCL-5, AUDIT-C, DAST-10) with auto-escalation to crisis services across the platform ecosystem</li>
<li>Built MAP-GAP continuous fidelity monitoring framework that will track Sankofa project outcomes across all three pillars using RE-AIM evaluation dimensions</li>
<li>Certified Community Health Worker Instructor -- directly relevant to training 20 Austin-based CHWs in the Bidirectional Knowledge Exchange curriculum</li>
</ul>

<h2>Professional Experience</h2>

<h3>President -- The Collaborative Advocate Foundation | 2025-Present</h3>
<ul>
<li>Founded 501(c)(3) nonprofit to dismantle structural barriers to health, economic mobility, and community wellbeing for BIPOC communities in Central Texas</li>
<li>Built and deployed 24 interconnected platforms: HerHealth Network (70 women's health conditions), Whole-Person Health (mental wellness with 6 clinical instruments), Mission Transition (veteran reintegration), ThriveUp Academy (workforce readiness), LifeBridge (CHW hub), SafeCogniCare (cognitive health), RPLICE (SDOH data intelligence), MentorConnect, and 16 additional specialized platforms</li>
<li>Developed AI-powered health navigation system serving communities in ZIP codes 78702, 78721, 78741, 78744 where chronic disease prevalence runs 40-60% above state baselines</li>
<li>Established Grant Command Center tracking 80+ funding opportunities with strategic alignment scoring</li>
</ul>

<h3>Public Health Social Scientist -- U.S. Federal Government (VA/DoD) | 2017-Present</h3>
<ul>
<li>Designed enterprise-level frameworks integrating implementation science with operational execution to improve healthcare delivery across federal systems</li>
<li>Trained Veterans Crisis Line responders in high-risk, time-sensitive crisis intervention requiring rapid decision-making and cultural competence</li>
<li>Community Readiness and Resilience Implementer (CR2I): Advised senior military leadership on resilience, readiness, and system-level performance; coordinated cross-functional stakeholders to implement behavioral health and prevention programs</li>
<li>Led initiatives improving outcomes related to social determinants of health, behavioral health, and population health management across veteran and military family populations</li>
</ul>

<h3>Founder and Principal Consultant -- Integrated Services and Solutions LLC | 2020-Present</h3>
<ul>
<li>Developed AGOS and RPLICE governance and decision-support platforms unifying strategy, data, and execution across organizations</li>
<li>Built AI-enabled systems accelerating decision-making and cross-functional collaboration for public and private sector clients across healthcare, emergency management, and workforce systems</li>
</ul>

